course: dictionary
lesson: 8096
title: Removable and the -able ending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word removable comes from remove, which means take away, and the ending -able, which means can be. So removable means can be taken off or taken out.
explain: Look at the context: «Some stable ankle and foot breaks, ones not likely to slip out of place, heal well in a removable boot instead of a cast.» A cast is fixed on and stays on. The word instead tells you the removable boot is different, so it must be one you can take off.
explain: The second meaning is about getting rid of something, like a stain. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «a boot you can take off» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Removable means it can be taken off or taken out.
fact: «Removable» can also mean it can be got rid of, like a stain.
fact: The ending -able means can be, so washable means can be washed and removable means can be removed.
fact: Removable covers, lids and batteries can be taken off, and removable stickers can be peeled away.
fact: Removable parts of toys may be a choking risk, so a grown-up should check them before a young child plays.
exercise: «Some stable ankle and foot breaks, ones not likely to slip out of place, heal well in a removable boot instead of a cast.» What does removable mean here? | *Able to be taken off | Made of glass | Very heavy | Fixed on for ever
exercise: A stain on your shirt is removable. What does this tell you? | *It can be got rid of | It cannot be washed | It is made of cloth | It will get bigger
exercise: What does the -able ending add to remove? | It means very, so removable means extremely removed | It means not, so removable means cannot be removed | It means again, so removable means removed twice | *It means can be, so removable means can be removed
test: Why is a removable lid useful on a jar? | *You can take it off to get at what is inside | It keeps the jar warm | It makes the jar lighter | It is stuck on for ever
test: A toy has removable parts. Why should a grown-up check them? | They make the toy float | They make the toy taste nice | *They may be a choking risk for a young child | They stop the toy from working
exam: Which word in «a removable boot instead of a cast» is the opposite idea to removable, meaning fixed in place? | boot | heal | instead | *cast
